.TH "DEDB DOSBOXCONF" "1" "2026-01-01" "0.0.14" "dedb dosboxconf Manual"
.SH NAME
dedb\-dosboxconf \- Show aspects of a DOSBox config, from dosbox.conf(s) or a game's launch...
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dedb dosboxconf
[OPTIONS] SOURCES...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show aspects of a DOSBox config, from dosbox.conf(s) or a game's
launch command line.
.PP
SOURCES is one or more dosbox.conf paths, or a single downloaded game
('gog:<id>' / 'archive:<id>', or a bare id with --backend) whose
resolved DOSBox command line is shown - an archive.org item has no
dosbox.conf, just the emularity command line. The game only needs to
be downloaded, not imported. With none of -a/-s/-g given, those three
aspects are shown; --issues is always opt-in. --cmdline prints the
whole `dosbox` command instead.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-b,\fP \-\-backend SCHEME
Read SOURCES as one bare game id for this backend, rather than dosbox.conf paths.
.TP
\fB\-\-profile\fP TEXT
Launch profile, for a gog:// game.
.TP
\fB\-a,\fP \-\-autoexec
Show the [autoexec] commands.
.TP
\fB\-s,\fP \-\-sblaster
Show Sound Blaster ([sblaster]) settings.
.TP
\fB\-g,\fP \-\-gus
Show Gravis Ultrasound ([gus]) settings.
.TP
\fB\-i,\fP \-\-issues
List the commands DOSEMU2 can't run as-is, grouped by severity.
.TP
\fB\-v,\fP \-\-verbose
With --issues, also show each autoexec line and what it is rewritten to.
.TP
\fB\-\-cmdline\fP
Print the `dosbox` command `dedb run --dosbox` would run, and stop.
